{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974408-stories-of-obsession","id":974408,"title":"Stories of Obsession","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-22T07:41:17-07:00","id":974408,"title":"Stories of Obsession","content":"Obsession is perhaps my favourite thing that's been introduced in 2nd edition. Anything that effectively encourages players to seek out the strange, weird and mysterious is a great idea in my book. Also the idea of PC's slowly falling down the rabbit hole as they try to solve the puzzle or indulge their obsession really appeals to me! It really adds a sense that even if you take the magic out of the equation, Mages are very different to your 'average' person.<br /> <br /> nfortunately I have yet to get a chance to play or run 2nd edition and this doesn't look likely to change any time soon, so I was hoping some folk here would be eager to share some stories of their characters or players Obsessions so I can see how this simple but fun new mechanic works in a real game? <br /> <br /> I also figure it will be good story fodder for future games (I ran 1st edition and will run 2nd sometime when I am not running Exalted 3e and have players open to the game). <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T06:53:23-07:00","id":975496,"title":"","content":"I like to resolve Obsessions that reward the mage, but also cost him dearly. One of our PCs, a Mastigoi hacker, had as his Obsession &quot;Infiltrate the enemy mage's Sanctum&quot;. While exploring said Sanctum, he activated a mirror that allowed the user to communicate with the Abyss. For a few precious seconds, he had an unadulterated link to an Abyssal Entity, which deeply disturbed him. For the rest of the Story he had the Spooked Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:06:37-07:00","id":975666,"title":"","content":"Obsessions are the player's way of telling the ST &quot;This is what I want in the game&quot;, just like Aspirations. They're things their character wants to chase and things the player wants them to chase. Personally, I like to make them reasonably broad.<br /> <br /> As I said in another thread, a fun tip for using Obsessions is to tell your players when a certain action will award an A-Beat, especially if it's something they wouldn't be inclined to normally do (but their character might want to anyway). Say, for example, a Mage with an Obsession about vampires finds one of the undead cruising a bar. If the PC manages to get the vamp's attention, such that the vamp's offering to go back to their place for a drink, the ST might say &quot;I'll give you an A-Beat if you allow the vampire to feed from you&quot;. Naturally, this might lead to the character developing Conditions that allow for further Beat gain.<br /> <br /> In-game, this is the Mage being curious enough about the whole thing that they'll risk their life to allow an undead nightmare to feed from them. In the process, they gain valuable insight; experiencing the strange sensations and developing new experiential knowledge. They might even watch with their unseen senses as the vampire feeds upon them.<br /> <br /> Then, inevitably, there will be fallout. The PC will have to deal with the aftermath of the feeding, even if it's entirely peaceful (peaceful as a vampire drinking your life away can be, at least). Perhaps it isn't, perhaps the vamp is too hungry, but that's depending on how far the ST wants to drag the Mage because, if it is, they've got a door open.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll give you another A-Beat if you go into the vampire's home during the day and observe it while it sleeps.&quot;<br /> <br /> And just like that, you're a supernatural home-invader for the sake of curiosity, who couldn't leave a(n admittedly parasitic) person alone.<br /> <br /> If the character survives, of course, you can then always say:<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll give you an A-Beat if your character manages to get the vampire to use their supernatural powers while using Focused Mage Sight.&quot;<br /> <br /> And suddenly they're thinking about provoking a vampire to anger because &quot;Hey, I know you're a vampire, let me see you use your powers&quot; is not really a good pick-up line.<br /> <br /> And on and on we go. Always make offers, and try not to specify that it has to be negative in some way. It's never &quot;Sneak into the vampire's home without their knowledge&quot;, but that's the inevitable path to follow. A reasonable and conscientious Mage could, in theory, politesse their way into the vampire's trust; enough to let them watch while they day-sleep, but that's so much effort and you <i>really</i> wanna see a vampire, and if no-one knows you were there, what's the harm, right?<br /> <br /> And thus the road to Obsession yawns wide because it's actually a fucking cliff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T14:30:26-07:00","id":975698,"title":"","content":"Thanks Axelgear, being able to neatly offer incentives that could lure a player down that road without it feeling forced or jarring is whats gotten me so excited about the notion of Obsession. Your example is exactly the kind of thing I was thinking of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T19:08:42-07:00","id":975764,"title":"","content":"Last session I Storytold a new Awakening (new Player in ChoD). She played an undergraduate law student of magical bloodline; ominous grandmother included. I had tottaly forgot about Obssessions until right after her Awakening in Pandemonium. She told me &quot;I feel like this has to do with my grandmother. Was she actually a witch on this City?&quot;. And then it hit me:<br /> <br /> <b>Obssession: &quot;Learn about magic of your Ancestors&quot;</b><br /> Give an Arcane Beat each time the player searches for her awakened family history (ex: Learn that grandma was an Adamant Sage) or encounters a setback due to actions of her ancestors (ex: family mages are in Counsil's &quot;black list&quot; due to past moraly questinable choices)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T00:47:35-07:00","id":975872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974408-stories-of-obsession?p=975698#post975698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Axelgear, being able to neatly offer incentives that could lure a player down that road without it feeling forced or jarring is whats gotten me so excited about the notion of Obsession. Your example is exactly the kind of thing I was thinking of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it! Hope things work out for you and your group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T01:04:03-07:00","id":975878,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a>, best piece of advise on running 2E games I read to this day!<br /> <br /> My only problem is that various Obsessions. like Aspirations, can quickly devolve in to 'character A do this, character B do that' and various party splitting, so I give 1 extra Obsession slot over the normal limit so all characters have one Obsession connecting to main chronicles plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T09:56:46-07:00","id":975987,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Wyrd! That's actually a good idea, too, as well. I have tried doing something similar and requiring a cabal Obsession as a requisite for having the Themed Cabal merit. In practice, that can be tricky, but I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T01:51:46-07:00","id":978270,"title":"","content":"A Cabal Obsession is a fantastic idea and it seems congruent to the way cabals have worked in the fiction (and in Dave's APs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}